{
  "about": "Decision 153-S3: the line a Shell launch may type into its terminal. The server (apps/server/src/agent/typed.rs) refuses anything in `refused` with typed_input_invalid before a start goes out; the host (apps/runtime/src/typed.rs) refuses it again and fails the start. Neither crate depends on the other: this file keeps them on one rule. A line is at most max_bytes UTF-8 bytes, holds no newline, carriage return or other control character, and none of the invisible or reordering characters U+200B-U+200F, U+202A-U+202E, U+2060-U+2069 and U+FEFF, so it never presses Enter and reads as it runs.",
